<title>USA: U.S. aluminum center shipments dip in Jan to Sept.</title>
<headline>U.S. aluminum center shipments dip in Jan to Sept.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipments from U.S. aluminum service centers in the first nine months of the year were 2.1 percent below the comparable period in 1995, the National Association of Aluminum Distributors reported.</p>
<p>According to NAAD's three-month moving average index, September shipments rose to 137.2 points from 133.9 points in August. Inventory fell slightly to 2.7 months of supply compared to 2.8 months in August.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
